# Python conventions (home-lab-pxe)

## Layout

- Application code lives under `src/`; pytest under `tests/`.
- Prefer new HTTP routes in `src/routes/` over growing `src/app.py`.
- Boot-policy and iPXE rendering belong in `src/boot/`. Cloud-init rendering belongs in `src/cloudinit/`. Windows unattend/Cloudbase-Init belong in `src/windows/`. Machine lifecycle and encrypted local accounts belong in `src/inventory/`.

## Style and lint

- Target Python 3.12; Ruff config in `pyproject.toml` (line length 120, rules E/F/I/UP).
- Run before commit: `python -m ruff check src tests` and `python -m ruff format --check src tests`.

## Security defaults

- Never log or return cloud-init user-data, unattend.xml secrets, Cloudbase-Init user-data, SSH private keys, local-account passwords, or session secrets.
- Fail fast when `SECRET_KEY` or `ENCRYPTION_KEY` are missing in production (`PXE_ALLOW_INSECURE_DEFAULTS=1` is test-only).
- Persist Linux root and Windows local Administrator username+password only as Fernet ciphertext; decrypt in memory at guest-seed render time. Passwords are write-only in the UI/API.
- Browser POSTs need CSRF; JSON API routes use session auth or an API key as appropriate.
- Treat MAC-based boot URLs as LAN-trust only; do not put secrets in iPXE scripts that a neighbor can TFTP/HTTP.

## Tests

- Use fixtures from `tests/conftest.py` for isolated SQLite and test settings.
- Mock DHCP/TFTP/dnsmasq and external image downloads; container/PXE behavior is covered by CI smoke.
- Name tests `tests/test_<module>.py` matching the module under test.

## Version and docs

- User-visible changes need `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` entries.
- New env vars need `.env.example` entries with safe placeholders.
